    "code": "# Python3 code for program to\n# cyclically rotate an array by one\n \n# Method for rotation\ndef rotate(arr, n):\n    x = arr[n - 1]\n     \n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i] = arr[i - 1];\n         \n    arr[0] = x;\n \n \n# Driver function\narr= [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\nn = len(arr)\nprint (\"Given array is\")\nfor i in range(0, n):\n    print (arr[i], end = ' ')\n \nrotate(arr, n)\n \nprint (\"\\nRotated array is\")\nfor i in range(0, n):\n    print (arr[i], end = ' ')\n \n# This article is contributed\n# by saloni1297",
